<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dalmatia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dalmatia is a historical region along the eastern Adriatic coast, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>. It came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule in the nineteenth century. Within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> it was one of the predominantly rural and less developed provinces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dalmatia.jpg" alt="Dalmatia" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DIREKTOR · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dalmatia_(Kotor).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
